.TH JANUSGATECTL 1 "August 2026" "JanusGate 0.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
janusgatectl \- administer a JanusGate appliance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B janusgatectl
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.br
.B janusgatectl
.B --version
.br
.B janusgatectl
.B --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B janusgatectl
is the non-interactive administration client for JanusGate.
By default, it performs the complete command set through the local control
socket, authenticated by privileged Unix peer credentials.
Local administration must run as root.
Specifying
.B --endpoint
selects the dedicated versioned remote HTTPS management API and requires
.BR --token-file ,
.BR --client-cert ,
and
.BR --client-key .
.PP
Inputs are bounded and validated before transmission.
JSON output is stable and suitable for automation.
Secret values are displayed only when an operation explicitly creates a
one-time secret.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --socket " path"
Use
.I path
as the local daemon control socket.
This transport is the default and accepts administrative requests only from
root.
The default is
.I /run/janusgate/control/control.sock
on Linux and
.I /var/run/janusgate/control/control.sock
on OpenBSD.
.TP
.BI --endpoint " URL"
Use the HTTPS management origin at
.IR URL .
The value must identify an HTTPS origin without a path, query, or fragment.
The appliance default is port 9443.
.TP
.BI --token-file " path"
Read one remote API bearer token from a private regular file.
The file must be owned by the current user and must not be writable by group
or other users. This option requires
.BR --endpoint .
.TP
.BI --passphrase-file " path"
Read a full-backup passphrase from a private regular file.
This avoids exposing the passphrase in process arguments.
.TP
.BI --client-cert " path"
Use the PEM client certificate at
.I path
for mandatory remote mutual TLS.
This option requires
.BR --endpoint .
.TP
.BI --client-key " path"
Use the PEM private key at
.IR path .
This option must be used with
.BR --client-cert
and requires
.BR --endpoint .
.TP
.BI --ca-file " path"
Trust the PEM certification authorities in
.I path
instead of the system trust store.
.TP
.BI --timeout " seconds"
Set the remote request timeout.
The accepted range is 1 through 300 seconds.
.TP
.B --json
Write one compact JSON value with stable field names.
.TP
.B --quiet
Suppress successful human-readable output.
Errors remain visible.
.TP
.B --verbose
Report transport and request details without printing secrets.
.TP
.B --yes
Confirm a destructive operation without interactive terminal input.
.TP
.B --include-private-key
Include the active server private key in a newly created encrypted full
backup.
.TP
.B --help
Display the complete command synopsis and exit.
.TP
.B --version
Display build version information and exit.
.SH STATUS COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Return readiness, active policy generation, and bounded packet counters.
.TP
.B health
Return daemon and privileged network-helper health.
.TP
.B stats
Return authenticated Prometheus metrics.
.SH NETWORK COMMANDS
.TP
.B network show
Display persistent and effective network state.
.TP
.BI "network validate " file
Validate the complete JSON network configuration in
.I file
without applying it.
.TP
.BI "network apply " file
Stage a revision-bound JSON network configuration.
The change rolls back automatically unless it is confirmed before the
reported deadline.
.TP
.BI "network set " file
Validate, stage, and confirm the JSON network configuration in one guarded
workflow.
.TP
.B network confirm
Confirm the pending network transaction after reading its current revision.
.TP
.B network rollback
Restore the pending network checkpoint after reading its current revision.
.SH POLICY COMMANDS
.TP
.B policy list
List global enforcement, groups, client scopes, and policy records.
.TP
.BI "policy mode " [file]
Read snapshot-wide enforcement, or replace it from a JSON document after
automatically retrieving the current revision.
.TP
.BI "policy statistics " [file]
Read detailed-statistics retention and lifetime traffic counters, or replace
retention from a JSON document after automatically retrieving the current
revision.
.TP
.BI "policy cleanup " preview|run
Preview expired policy-impact detail or remove one bounded batch.
Running cleanup requires interactive confirmation or
.BR --yes .
Lifetime aggregates are preserved.
.TP
.BI "policy show " "kind id"
Display one
.B domain
or
.B destination
record, policy
.B group
or client
.B scope
mode.
.TP
.BI "policy add " "kind file"
Create a
.B domain
or
.B destination
record from a strict JSON object.
.TP
.BI "policy update " "kind id file"
Replace one revision-bound policy record.
.TP
.BI "policy remove " "kind id"
Remove one policy record after retrieving its current revision.
.TP
.BI "policy analyze " "kind id"
Display lifetime hits, retained client impact, traffic percentage, and
conservative relationship findings for one
.B domain
or
.B destination
rule.
.TP
.BI "policy explain " file
Explain a policy decision without changing state. The compatible
.B policy simulate
spelling is also accepted.
.PP
Blocking rules, sources, groups, client scopes, and the global policy mode can
use persistent
.B observe
enforcement. An observed block is recorded as a would-block and allowed; it
does not expire and cannot strengthen an allow decision into a block.
.TP
.BI "domain block " domain
Create a global DNS block rule for
.IR domain .
.TP
.BI "domain allow " domain
Create a global DNS allow rule for
.IR domain .
.TP
.BI "domain remove " id
Remove an explicit domain rule after retrieving its current revision.
.SH SOURCE COMMANDS
.TP
.B blocklist list
List configured blocklist sources.
.TP
.BI "blocklist import " "source file"
Import bounded content from
.I file
into the named local source through the bounded management queue and wait for
completion.
.TP
.B blocklist export
Export the normalized active blocklist as JSON or one domain per line.
.TP
.B source list
List local and remote source configuration and update state.
.TP
.BI "source add " file
Create a source from a strict JSON object.
.TP
.BI "source update " "id file"
Replace one source at its current revision.
.TP
.BI "source refresh " id
Queue one remote-source refresh at its current revision and wait for its
retained result.
.TP
.BI "source enable " id
Enable one source at its current revision.
.TP
.BI "source disable " id
Disable one source at its current revision.
.SH EVENT AND AUDIT COMMANDS
.TP
.RI "events [" query ]
List stable operational events.
The optional query uses API query syntax such as
.BR "severity=error&limit=20" .
.TP
.RI "audit [" query ]
List immutable audit records.
.TP
.B audit verify
Verify every link in the persistent audit hash chain.
.SH ACCESS COMMANDS
.TP
.B user list
List local user accounts.
.TP
.BI "user add " file
Create a local user from a strict JSON object.
If standard input is a terminal, the password is read without echo and
replaces the object's password member.
.TP
.BI "user update " "id file"
Replace the role and mutable state of one local user.
.TP
.BI "user disable " id
Disable one user after retrieving its current revision.
.TP
.BI "user password " "id file"
Reset a user's password at its current revision.
.TP
.BI "user totp " id
Disable a user's TOTP enrollment at its current revision.
.TP
.B token list
List API-token metadata without token secrets.
.TP
.BI "token create " file
Create a scoped API token and display its secret once.
.TP
.BI "token revoke " id
Revoke an API token.
.SH CERTIFICATE COMMANDS
.TP
.B certificate show
Inspect the active server certificate.
.TP
.BI "certificate install " file
Validate and atomically install certificate material from a strict JSON
object.
.TP
.BI "certificate csr " file
Create a private key on the appliance and return its certificate signing
request.
.SH MUTUAL-TLS COMMANDS
.TP
.B mtls ca show
Inspect the client certification-authority bundle trusted by the remote API.
.TP
.BI "mtls ca install " file
Validate and atomically install a PEM bundle containing only root and
intermediate certification authorities.
.TP
.B mtls ca remove
Remove the client trust bundle and disable the remote API listener.
.TP
.B mtls mapping list
List active and revoked client-certificate mappings.
.TP
.BI "mtls mapping add " "file user id"
Map the leaf certificate in PEM
.I file
to the existing user
.IR id .
.TP
.BI "mtls mapping add " "file role role"
Map the leaf certificate in PEM
.I file
to the named
.B administrator,
.BR operator ,
or
.B auditor
role.
.TP
.BI "mtls mapping revoke " id
Revoke a client-certificate mapping immediately.
.SH BACKUP COMMANDS
.TP
.B backup create configuration
Create a configuration backup without authentication secrets and wait for the
bounded job to complete.
.TP
.B backup create full
Create an authenticated encrypted portable full backup containing the
database, TOTP protection key, and public client CA bundle.
A passphrase is read from
.B --passphrase-file
or securely from the terminal.
.TP
.BI "backup inspect " id
Verify and display stored backup metadata.
.TP
.BI "backup export " "id file"
Verify a stored archive and write it to a new absolute private path.
This operation is available only through the local socket and never overwrites
an existing file.
.TP
.BI "backup import " file
Validate an archive from an absolute private path, copy it into protected
storage, and assign it a new local ID.
This operation is available only through the local socket.
.TP
.BI "backup restore " id
Validate a backup, show the dry-run comparison, and apply it only after
confirmation. Both phases wait for their bounded management jobs. An applied
restore excludes other management writes and creates an audited checkpoint.
A current full restore replaces users, sessions, tokens, TOTP credentials and
their protection key, the public client CA bundle, and client-certificate
mappings; run full recovery restores through the local socket because remote
authorization may be replaced before the result is read.
.SH SYSTEM COMMANDS
.TP
.B diagnostics create
Create and save a bounded sanitized diagnostic archive after its management job
completes.
.TP
.B logging show
Show active structured-logging configuration and bounded counters.
.TP
.BI "logging set " file
Revision-check and activate the logging configuration in a strict JSON file.
Debug and trace levels must include an automatic expiration.
.TP
.B logging traces
Show the bounded in-memory diagnostic trace window.
.TP
.B config validate
Validate all persistent runtime configuration.
.TP
.B config reload
Validate and atomically publish persistent runtime configuration.
.TP
.B service restart
Restart the policy service after explicit confirmation.
.TP
.B system reboot
Reboot the appliance after explicit confirmation.
.TP
.B system shutdown
Power off the appliance after explicit confirmation.
.TP
.B ping
Check the local versioned control socket.
.TP
.B policy reload
Request a local policy reload through the control socket.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The operation completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
A local validation, input/output, or non-specific API failure occurred.
.TP
.B 2
The command line or an input document was invalid.
.TP
.B 3
Authentication or authorization failed.
.TP
.B 4
The requested revision conflicted with current state.
.TP
.B 5
The remote service or a required appliance component was unavailable.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/janusgate/control/control.sock
Default local control socket on Linux.
.TP
.I /var/run/janusgate/control/control.sock
Default local control socket on OpenBSD.
.TP
.I /etc/janusgate/
Persistent appliance configuration and certificate directory.
.TP
.I /var/lib/janusgate/backups/
Private backup archive directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo janusgatectl status

sudo janusgatectl domain block example.org

janusgatectl --endpoint https://192.168.77.1:9443 \\
  --token-file /root/.config/janusgate/token \\
  --client-cert /root/.config/janusgate/client.crt \\
  --client-key /root/.config/janusgate/client.key status

janusgatectl --endpoint https://192.168.77.1:9443 \\
  --token-file /root/.config/janusgate/token \\
  --client-cert /root/.config/janusgate/client.crt \\
  --client-key /root/.config/janusgate/client.key \\
  network apply network.json

janusgatectl --endpoint https://192.168.77.1:9443 \\
  --token-file /root/.config/janusgate/token \\
  --client-cert /root/.config/janusgate/client.crt \\
  --client-key /root/.config/janusgate/client.key \\
  --yes system reboot
.fi
.SH SECURITY
Keep token, private-key, passphrase, and input files private.
Local administration is equivalent to root appliance access and is accepted
only from a root Unix-socket peer.
Remote administration is accepted only on the dedicated mutual-TLS listener.
The client certificate must chain to an appliance trust anchor, have an active
leaf-fingerprint mapping, and match the bearer token's user or role.
Prefer
.B --ca-file
or the system trust store over disabling certificate verification; the client
does not provide an insecure mode.
Use the narrowest API-token scopes required by automation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR janusgate-setup (8),
.BR janusgated (8),
.BR janusgate-web (8),
.BR janusgate-netd (8)
